   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\nestablishing a license to sell liquor on premises commonly known as a\nfor-profit club",
    "basePrintNo": "S652",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S652-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §64-f, amd §§110-b & 17, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S652A\n\nSPONSOR: GIANARIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\nestablishing a license to sell liquor on premises commonly known as a\nfor-profit club\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would amend Alcoholic Beverage Control Law to establish a new\nlicense category to allow For-Profit Clubs to operate solely for recre-\national, social, patriotic, political, benevolent, communal workspace,\ncorporate dining space, or athletic purposes. The bill also provides for\nthe license regulatory structure and an annual fee of $20,000.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new § 64-F to the alcohol beverage control law to\nestablish a new license category to allow \"For-Profit Clubs.\"\n\nSection 2 amends § 110-b to require community notification for individ-\nuals seeking For-Profit Club licenses.\n\nSection 3 and 4 amend Section 17-a of the alcohol beverage control law\nto allow the State Liquor Authority to enforce capabilities related to\nFor-Profit Club licenses.\n\nSection 5 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would create a new 'for-profit club' license within the\nAlcoholic Beverage Control Law. This change will create a new category\nfor those interested in opening a club in New York and will allow enti-\nties that have been authorized under the current club license as not-\nfor-profits the option to modify their licenses. This legislation would\nsupport the nightlife and hospitality industry, which is an important\neconomic driver for the state.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-2024: A.10381/S.9464: Referred to Economic Development / PASSED\nSENATE\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTBD\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
